A||||11||SCCA FIERO||X BOX - Project Gotham Racing!!||||1||
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||12-30-2001||06:22 PM||||I just bought an XBox and PGR.<P>I must say I am floored with this game and the XBox!<P>Only been playing for a couple hours,but it like watching a race on TV! When the car peels out, the tires smoke, the black marks stay there for the whole race. When you hit the wall, the car gets dented and the lights will go out if hit as well. You can see the driver, the brake discs (they get red got) and even the caliper. If the car hits the ground it shoots sparks. It's so real. If you lock the brakes, the tires will stop spinning too.<P>The demos are totally amazing! This game just rocks! Better than any Gran Turismo game.<P>Gotta go play some more...<P><P>------------------<BR>-Chris <BR>88 Fiero Coupe (V6 & fastback conversion)<BR><B>Fear is a good motivator. That and second place.</B>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Neal||12-30-2001||06:43 PM||||I know what you mean about PGR, i must of played it for 4 hours straight when i visited a frient who has it...<P>VERY good looking game, VERY addicting game...||||reg||14
Z||000002||banditbalz||12-30-2001||06:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SCCA FIERO:<BR><B> This game just rocks! Better than any Gran Turismo game.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I don't know, sounds kinda boring. Batman and Robin just don't do it for me anymore...<P>Now Grand Turismo 3 on Playstation2 just rocks!  It's more of a simulator with REAL physics. Imagine having control over ride height, caster, camber and toe... Imagine choosing from over 8 racing tire compounds.<P>It doesn't get any better than GT3 <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||West Coast Fiero||12-30-2001||06:49 PM||||I have gotten up to the Lancer EVO, but in arcade mode, hard, Tokyo is kicking my ass<P> I have no idea how that damn blue SLK 320 gets out in front and maintains the lead, I tried to drive it and it handles like a Mack truck<P> but if you want every track and every carm in every color<P> start a new driver and call him " Nosliw " ( case sensitive )<P> ...enjoy and let me know what you think, I noticed that the XBOX supports Ethernet so it looks like I will be bringing it to the shop and racing and body else out there with PGR, I'll have to let you know when we get online<P> But right now Im ready to tear the thing open and start mods - I think a spec GVA3 video card might replace the stock unit, souns card may not hurt either<P> but not to bad for a 733Mh processor  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||12-30-2001||08:28 PM||||MMMMM F50! Thanks, Eric!||||reg||1
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||12-30-2001||08:30 PM||||Just noticed in the convertible cars you can see the guy shifting or reaching for the e brake.<P>Did you watch the demo of the F50? Amazing!||||reg||1
Z||000006||West Coast Fiero||12-30-2001||09:06 PM||||the F50 is an oversteering B*tch, when going around a turn TAP the brake button ( feather it ) and get of the gas, then once out of the turn jump on the gas<P> I found that more often than not I use the MINI for Kudos as it slides its ass around a turn when you hit the e-brake, very fun car to drive<P> With that code you will see just how good you are when you go to race at the highest level ( world championchip I believe ) vs. other F50 - I give you major props if you come in 3rd or higher, major pain in the ass<P> but to me the hardest track so far is the Tei-mae hairpin, when you go to turn into the narrow allew ways, thats where I always get passed by that damned SLK<P> and give up any thought of trying to use the Camaro for a race, overpowered and underhandling POS, same as the Viper - I hope the programing variables arent the same as the real car, cause that would mean that the Porche is a piece of crap as well.<P>best of luck on the game, keep me posted on your score<P> on a side note, I went out and got Gran Tourismo 1 for my PS yesterday for the hell of it, always liked the game but its graphics truly are Atari compared to XBOX, just wish that PGR had options to chance everything about the car as GT does<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000007||SCCA FIERO||12-30-2001||11:18 PM||||Without the code I am struggling through Hard. Trying to make 3rd in San Fransico is proving to be a pain. I have only had it a few hours though. That SS Camaro is good for Kudos though... lots of oversteer.<P>My wife went to Wal-Mart and bought the DVD adapter/remote and Dead or Alive 3. Right now it's her turn to play the XBOX. She insists I let her play that game for a few days before I play it so she can whip my butt (not likely...lol).||||reg||1
Z||000008||SCCA FIERO||12-30-2001||11:25 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B><P> <BR> on a side note, I went out and got Gran Tourismo 1 for my PS yesterday for the hell of it, always liked the game but its graphics truly are Atari compared to XBOX, just wish that PGR had options to chance everything about the car as GT does<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have GT1 and GT2 for the Playstation. It's nice but the graphics suck compared to the X. Also the laws a gravity seem to not apply to the cars (mostly the AI cars).<P>I do wish the cars were tunable/adjustable in PGR, but it's still the most awesome game I have played based on the fact it just looks real. <P>My cousin is gonna get the PS2 and GT3 soon. I can't wait to play that.<P>So far I am on the 3rd set of races (Hard) with the Camaro SS unlocked. I can't seem to get 3rd - much less 1st in any of the races. I'll keep plugging away at it.<P>How many cars are there in the whole game?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 12-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||West Coast Fiero||12-30-2001||11:56 PM||||for Hard, use the Mini for San Fransisco, you will be able to out steer everything, the beetle is also a good choice.<P> As far as cars, there are no secret cars that I know abaout - just everything from the Mini to the F50<P> I want to go and get the DVD setup, how much did you pay for it?<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000010||SCCA FIERO||12-31-2001||12:53 AM||||At Wal-Mart it was $29.99. At the game store I bought the XBOX, the adapter/remote was 34.99. <P>I use the Bettle... it's AWD! Haven't tried the Mini.<P>With the hard drive and an internet connection, you think it will be possible to d/l new cars/tracks?<P>I already made a kickin' soundtrack. This thing has the neatest bells and whistles!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||West Coast Fiero||12-31-2001||01:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SCCA FIERO:<BR><B>At Wal-Mart it was $29.99. At the game store I bought the XBOX, the adapter/remote was 34.99. <P>I use the Bettle... it's AWD! Haven't tried the Mini.<P>With the hard drive and an internet connection, you think it will be possible to d/l new cars/tracks?<P>I already made a kickin' soundtrack. This thing has the neatest bells and whistles!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>my god, I didnt even think about downloads..<B>SCHWEEEEEEEEEEEEEET!!!!</B><P>for the soundtrack you want to listen to Kittie and Salivia primarily, gold medals and first place wins happen with this music =-)<P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
